0,0.27)" title="supply still present on the test (MTM p.158)"><b>0.8</b><br><small>supply still present on the test</small></td><td class="r" style="background:rgba(214,40,40,0.27)" title="supply still present on the test (MTM p.158)"><b>0.8</b><br><small>supply still present on the test</small></td><td class="r" style="background:rgba(214,40,40,0.33)" title="failed test in a weak market (MTM p.158; WTW v1 p.9)"><b>1.0</b><br><small>failed test in a weak market</small></td><td class="r" style="background:rgba(214,40,40,0.27)" title="supply still present after the climax - expect more testing (MTM p.158)"><b>0.8</b><br><small>supply still present after the climax - expect more testing</small></td></tr><tr><td><span class="vsam m">SQ</span><b>Squat bar (high volume, narrow spread)</b></td><td class="r" style="background:rgba(214,40,40,0.13)" title="heavy volume, little progress near the highs: supply meeting demand (effort vs result) (MTM p.39, p.111)"><b>0.4</b><br><small>heavy volume, little progress near the highs: supply meeting…</small></td><td class="r" style="background:rgba(214,40,40,0.27)" title="heavy volume, no progress, with weakness in the background (MTM p.111)"><b>0.8</b><br><small>heavy volume, no progress, with weakness in the background</small></td><td class="r" style="background:var(--panel2)" title="heavy volume, no progress inside the range (MTM p.39)"><b>0.3</b><br><small>heavy volume, no progress inside the range</small></td><td class="r" style="background:rgba(31,157,58,0.20)" title="heavy volume, no progress in a decline: selling being absorbed (MTM p.39, p.142)"><b>0.6</b><br><small>heavy volume, no progress in a decline: selling being absorb…</small></td><td class="r" style="background:rgba(31,157,58,0.27)" title="heavy volume, no progress after strength: absorption (MTM p.142)"><b>0.8</b><br><small>heavy volume, no progress after strength: absorption</small></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="meth">Weight (0.3 = minor … 3.0 = major; colour = polarity, green strength / red weakness). Hover a cell for the reason and page reference. n/a = the sign is only defined in the other contexts (a test in a rising market needs an uptrend; a buying climax needs a prior rise).</p></div><h2 class="bigsec" id="pairs">🔁 Same sign, different context <small>clearest desk example of each sign in an uptrend vs a downtrend, last 15 sessions: same bar shape, different weight</small></h2><div class="panel"><div class="tscroll"><table class="mini" id="vex"><thead><tr><th>Ticker</th><th>Sign</th><th>Context</th><th>Significance</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-tk="VREX"><td class="tkc"><b>VREX</b></td><td><span class="vsam m">ND</span>No demand 06/10</td><td>uptrend</td><td class="r">0.29<span class="vsat low" title="context-weighted significance">low</span></td><td class="why">inside an uptrend - often just a pause on a pullback (lack of professional interest, not selling); at resistance / new highs</td></tr><tr data-tk="ALB"><td class="tkc"><b>ALB</b></td><td><span class="vsam m">ND</span>No demand 06/10</td><td>downtrend</td><td class="r">1.12<span class="vsat moderate" title="context-weighted significance">mod</span></td><td class="why">no demand in a downtrend: significant</td></tr><tr data-tk="PBF"><td class="tkc"><b>PBF</b></td><td><span class="vsam p">NS</span>No supply 06/10</td><td>uptrend</td><td class="r">1.20<span class="vsat moderate" title="context-weighted significance">mod</span></td><td class="why">no selling pressure inside an uptrend: significant</td></tr><tr data-tk="GTX"><td class="tkc"><b>GTX</b></td><td><span class="vsam p">NS</span>No supply 24/09</td><td>downtrend</td><td class="r">0.42<span class="vsat low" title="context-weighted significance">low</span></td><td class="why">in a downtrend a quiet down bar alone rarely turns it; at support / new lows</td></tr><tr data-tk="FTRE"><td class="tkc"><b>FTRE</b></td><td><span class="vsam m">UT</span>Upthrust 06/10</td><td>uptrend</td><td class="r">0.99<span class="vsat moderate" title="context-weighted significance">mod</span></td><td class="why">inside an uptrend with strength behind it an upthrust is &#x27;in the wrong place&#x27;; at resistance / new highs</td></tr><tr data-tk="AIN"><td class="tkc"><b>AIN</b></td><td><span class="vsam m">UT</span>Upthrust 05/10</td><td>downtrend</td><td class="r">2.12<span class="vsat high" title="context-weighted significance">HIGH</span></td><td class="why">an upthrust in a downtrend - the highest-probability weakness</td></tr><tr data-tk="FRHC"><td class="tkc"><b>FRHC</b></td><td><span class="vsam p">SV</span>Stopping volume 02/10</td><td>uptrend</td><td class="r">2.93<span class="vsat high" title="context-weighted significance">HIGH</span></td><td class="why">in an uptrend with buying behind it: bullish; at support / new lows</td></tr><tr data-tk="LQDA"><td class="tkc"><b>LQDA</b></td><td><span class="vsam p">SV</span>Stopping volume 01/10</td><td>downtrend</td><td class="r">0.70<span class="vsat moderate" title="context-weighted significance">mod</span></td><td class="why">in a downtrend it usually only pauses the fall; at support / new lows</td></tr><tr data-tk="NTSK"><td class="tkc"><b>NTSK</b></td><td><span class="vsam p">T</span>Test 05/10</td><td>uptrend</td><td class="r">1.20<span class="vsat moderate" title="context-weighted significance">mod</span></td><td class="why">a low-volume test with strength behind it: supply is drying up</td></tr><tr data-tk="RELY"><td class="tkc"><b>RELY</b></td><td><span class="vsam p">T</span>Test 01/10</td><td>downtrend</td><td class="r">0.32<span class="vsat low" title="context-weighted significance">low</span></td><td class="why">a test in a weak market: only counts if price responds at once</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<h2 class="bigsec" id="method">📖 Signs &amp; method</h2><div class="panel"><div class="vsa-legend"><div><span class="vsam p">SC</span><b>Selling climax</b> <small>(strength)</small></div><div><span class="vsam p">SV</span><b>Stopping volume</b> <small>(strength)</small></div><div><span class="vsam p">BH</span><b>Bag holding</b> <small>(strength)</small></div><div><span class="vsam p">SO</span><b>Shakeout</b> <small>(strength)</small></div><div><span class="vsam p">T</span><b>Test</b> <small>(strength)</small></div><div><span class="vsam p">T</span><b>Test in a rising market</b> <small>(strength)</small></div><div><span class="vsam p">NS</span><b>No supply</b> <small>(strength)</small></div><div><span class="vsam p">ER</span><b>Effort to rise</b> <small>(strength)</small></div><div><span class="vsam p">AB</span><b>Absorption volume</b> <small>(strength)</small></div><div><span class="vsam m">BC</span><b>Buying climax</b> <small>(weakness)</small></div><div><span class="vsam m">UT</span><b>Upthrust</b> <small>(weakness)</small></div><div><span class="vsam m">PU</span><b>Pseudo-upthrust</b> <small>(weakness)</small></div><div><span class="vsam m">ND</span><b>No demand</b> <small>(weakness)</small></div><div><span class="vsam m">EM</span><b>End of a rising market</b> <small>(weakness)</small></div><div><span class="vsam m">EF</span><b>Effort to fall</b> <small>(weakness)</small></div><div><span class="vsam m">FT</span><b>Possible failed test (supply present)</b> <small>(weakness)</small></div><div><span class="vsam z">SQ</span><b>Squat bar (high volume, narrow spread)</b> <small>(context)</small></div></div><p class="meth"><b>Bar measures:</b> spread = high−low ÷ average of the prior 20 bars (wide ≥ 1.25×, narrow ≤ 0.75×); close position 0 (low) – 1 (high); volume ÷ prior 20-bar average (ultra high ≥ 2×, high ≥ 1.3×, low ≤ 0.8×, ultra low ≤ 0.5×); up/down bar = close vs prior close. <b>Key rules:</b> selling climax = wide down bar to a new 20-bar low on ≥ 2× volume after a decline, closing off the lows (or next bar up); stopping volume = heavy down bar in a reaction closing in its upper half, any spread (meaning set by trend: bullish in an uptrend, only a pause in a downtrend); no supply / no demand = narrow down / up bar on volume below the prior two bars; test = dips under the prior low, closes in the top 40% on low volume; test in a rising market (Holmes) = narrow down bar closing on the low on very low volume inside the prior bar, in an uptrend; upthrust = new short-term high, wide spread, closes in the lower quarter; buying climax = wide up bar into new highs on ≥ 2× volume closing mid/low after a run; end of a rising market = narrow up bar on ≥ 2× volume at new highs. <b>Context brain:</b> every sign is read against the trend at the bar before it (50-day slope, price vs 50-day, 20- vs 50-day, swing highs/lows; a ±15% 20-bar move overrides), the background (a climactic strength / weakness sign in the prior 30 bars) and the location (near range support / resistance, new 20-bar highs / lows). The context matrix above gives each sign × context a weight, polarity and reason (Williams / Holmes page refs); significance = bar match × weight × location. One context modifier: no demand in a downtrend / weak background followed within 5 bars by an upthrust is raised ×1.6 (Holmes p.81). Multi-bar sequences are Phase 2 and switched off. Balance 0–100 = recency-weighted sum of context-weighted signs plus the up-vs-down-bar volume ratio (≥ 60 strength, ≤ 40 weakness). Thresholds are desk calibration (Williams/Holmes publish none); pseudo-upthrust and squat are marked unverified in the method file. Confirmation uses the next bar, so older signs carry one bar of hindsight; today's bar is "awaiting next bar".</p><p class="meth">Sources: Tom Williams, <i>Master the Markets</i> (TradeGuider) and <i>That Was The Week</i>; Gavin Holmes, <i>Trading in the Shadow of the Smart Money</i> (page refs in the matrix; rules paraphrased). Price data to 2026-10-07; setup windows from the scan of 2026-10-07.</p></div>
